On Mon, Feb 17, 2003 at 02:55:43PM +0100, Heid Oliver wrote:
>
> I just put that shiny new ATI Radeon 9000 PCI into an UP2000+, but I
> didn't even get the inital blue SRM console. It looks like SRM
> (version 5.8-81) seems unable to recognize the radeon card ( I
> booted into SRM with a second video card). Is this a known issue, or
> am I just doing something wrong? Any help much appreciated!

Sigh...

I hate to rain on the parade, but the SRM console on UP2000+ seems
to be incapable of handling the BIOS on the more recent ATI cards.
Very recently there was a failure for it to work on a PCI 7500, which
was a very unpleasant surprise... :-(

One possible workaround: put the 9000 on the second PCI bus, then
wait for XFree86 4.3.0 to show up, as it has bus "domains" which
should help it to work from the non-zero buses...

