If you put it on pci bus 0, you may be able to have xorg post the card
when it loads using x86emu.  you could use a serial console for
booting purposes and hope xorg can post the card when it starts.  I
have a PCI 9000 as well that only works in alphabios for console
access, however, I've not tried my suggestion so it may work.  The
9000s are the fastest PCI boards ATI made (note there are also 9200
and 9250 PCI boards, but they tend to be the slower SE variants and
the only difference between 9000 and 92xx boards was support for AGP
8x, which is irrelevant here).  the 9100 would be a faster chip as it
is a full R200, however, I'm not sure anyone made PCI 9100s.

