> In that case, you might try it on bus 1 and use the serial port for console.

With the later SRM consoles on multi-bus machines like DS20/DS20E/ES40
and the TITAN boxes (DS15/DS25/ES45), it will try to run the BIOS on
the first VGA it finds, whatever bus that happens to be on (starting
with bus #0).

It's not clear whether the SRM in a UP2000 will do that, but it'd be
safer to try a dumb VGA in bus #0 if you plan on putting the
problematic card in bus #1.

Godd luck.

 --Jay++

